Subject: fix(run): resolve the agents repo and status comments against the configured host

Several places address github.com by name, so on any other host they leave the
appliance and are refused with credentials that were never meant for them:

  ! Could not resolve fullsend-ai/agents@main: 401 Bad credentials
  Error: resolving agent "triage": no config and agents-repo fallback unavailable
  ! Failed to post completion status: create issue comment on #79: 401 Bad credentials

An agent with no local definition is fetched from fullsend-ai/agents at run
time: the CLI resolves the repository to a commit through the forge API, then
downloads the harness from a raw URL. The API half used a bare gh.New, which
targets api.github.com regardless of GITHUB_API_URL. The status comment a run
posts about itself used the same constructor. Both now use
newGitHubLiveClient, which honours that variable and still leaves the token
optional, as the agents fallback requires because that repository is public.

The raw half is not the same host swap. github.com serves raw bytes from
raw.githubusercontent.com, while an enterprise install has no second hostname
and serves them from the appliance at <host>/<owner>/<repo>/raw/<ref>/<path>.
Derive the prefix from GITHUB_SERVER_URL using that convention.

The fetch policy's domain allowlist named only github.com's two hosts, so even
a correctly built URL was refused. Add the configured forge host to the default
allowlist, derived from the same variable, so the allowlist follows the forge
the run is already pointed at rather than widening independently.

All of these keep the public hosts, so behaviour on github.com is unchanged.

Breadboard note: patches Go source, so it belongs to the build patch list in
deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh rather than the mirror list; the mirror
patches files a workflow reads at run time, and these do not survive
compilation. Written to be sent upstream as-is. Add a DCO sign-off before
submitting it as a human-authored change.

